.TH CLEARMIC-CLI 1 "October 2026" "ClearMic 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clearmic-cli \- local microphone enhancement tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clearmic-cli
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
ClearMic provides local microphone discovery, explicit A/B capture tests, WAV processing, and (on Linux) a PipeWire real-time service that exposes processed audio as a virtual microphone.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B devices
List available microphone sources.
.TP
.B record-test \fIseconds original.wav processed.wav\fR [\fIdevice-id\fR]
Capture up to 30 seconds and write the original and processed samples for manual comparison.
.TP
.B serve
Continuously process the default PipeWire microphone and expose the result as ClearMic Virtual Microphone. Keep the command running while another application uses the virtual source. Stop with Ctrl+C.
.TP
.B process \fIinput.wav output.wav\fR
Apply the offline processor to supported 48 kHz PCM16 WAV audio.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Linux audio commands require a running PipeWire server and an available capture source. This CLI package does not install or configure a graphical desktop application.
.SH PRIVACY
Audio is processed locally. Recording files are created only by the explicit record-test command.
.SH AUTHOR
ClearMic contributors
